Z||000000||WisconsinGT||06-19-2000||11:28 PM||||First, I put in an ECM from a Formula with 66,000 miles. (Trying to trouble shoot my Rich mixture problem.) After the install I noticed a big difference in my idle. It was missing at idle but not any more. Also, I noticed that the IAC Valve set much quicker then before. Overall the car runs much better. But it still runs rich. Oh well, I think I have narrowed it down to the fuel system. <P>Second, went with a friend to check out a 1989 Toyota MR2. It was supercharged. WOW! What an experience. Talk about low end torque. It had balls. I wonder what would have happened to the Fiero in 89?||||reg||1
